# #725: the local entry-point supertool's own SessionStart hook creates at
# the repo root -- git-ignored here (tracked) rather than only in this one
# machine's local .git/info/exclude, so an ordinary `git add`/`git add -A`
# in a pull request branch will not silently track a file at this path (a
# contributor can still force it with `git add -f`, which .gitignore alone
# never blocks -- the actual guard against running whatever lands here is
# the rule layer no longer recommending `./supertool` at all, see
# tools/01-oss/00-README.md and supertool-required.md).
/supertool

# Local Claude Code state (machine scope, never shared)
.claude/settings.json
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/jit-context/.discovery/
.max/
